
# Air Quality Forecasting Using LSTM

## Project Overview
This project explores time-series forecasting using a Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) neural network and historical air-quality sensor data.

## Objectives
- Preprocess air-quality data.
- Train an LSTM forecasting model.
- Forecast sensor readings, temperature, and humidity.
- Evaluate model performance.

## Dataset
The project uses the AirQualityUCI Excel dataset.

## Technologies
- Python
- Jupyter Notebook
- Pandas and NumPy
- Matplotlib
- Scikit-learn
- TensorFlow / Keras

## Project Files
- `AQI_Forecasting.ipynb`: Main notebook
- `AirQualityUCI.xlsx`: Dataset
- `requirements.txt`: Python dependencies
- `.gitignore`: Files excluded from version control

## How to Run
1. Clone or download this repository.
2. Install dependencies using `pip install -r requirements.txt`.
3. Open `AQI_Forecasting.ipynb` in Jupyter Notebook.
4. Ensure the Excel dataset is in the expected location.
5. Run the notebook cells in order.

## Evaluation
Model metrics and plots should be added after running the notebook.

## Limitations
A sensor-based prediction is not automatically an official Air Quality Index (AQI). Official AQI estimation requires suitable pollutant measurements and a validated calculation method.
